<section id="methods" class="level2" data-number="1">
<h2 data-number="1" class="anchored" data-anchor-id="methods"><span class="header-section-number">1</span> Methods</h2>
<ul>
<li>We match AVENIR and MORDOR village lists in two stages, since village names in the two source lists frequently differ by spelling, transliteration, or diacritics: fuzzy name matching, followed by spatial distance verification.</li>
<li>Candidate name pairs are generated using Jaro-Winkler string distance (<code>method = "jw"</code>), which tolerates minor spelling variation while remaining sensitive to a shared prefix. Candidates exceeding a string distance of <code>0.15</code> are excluded before spatial verification.</li>
<li>Each surviving candidate is verified against the geographic distance between coordinates, projected to UTM zone 32N (EPSG:32632) rather than computed in geographic coordinates (EPSG:4326). Candidates beyond <code>1</code> km are excluded.</li>
<li>AVENIR villages with exactly one candidate passing both thresholds are matched directly. Villages with more than one passing candidate are resolved to the closest-name candidate where that resolution is unambiguous (no exact string-distance tie, no collision with another AVENIR village’s resolved match).</li>
<li><code>site_code</code> (AVENIR) and <code>grappe</code> (MORDOR) serve as primary keys throughout, since village names are not unique within the AVENIR list.</li>
<li>Distance to the nearest MORDOR village (<code>dist_nearest_mordor_km</code>) is computed for every AVENIR village independently of match status, via nearest-feature lookup in the same projected CRS — unmatched villages still carry a meaningful distance rather than a missing value.</li>
</ul>
</section>
